<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">măthēsis</span></b> , is
		(with the second syll. short: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">involvit măthĕsi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 893 al.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 5, 131</span></i>),
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάθησις</span> (lit.,
			knowledge, science; hence, in partic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The mathematics, mathesis</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrifariae mathesis januae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 1, 45</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 3,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Astrology</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mathesin scire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Spart. Hadr. 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ael. Vel. 3 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; Firm. Math. 1 praef. <i>init.</i>; <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2,
		479</span></i>.</div>
